# Copy to .env and paste your key below — that is the only edit needed.
# Free key from https://aistudio.google.com
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=

# gemini | fake
#   gemini = a real model (needs the key above)
#   fake   = the scripted deterministic model used by the tests; with this set,
#            chat requests return an error instead of talking to a model.
# Note: `npm test` installs its own scripted model, so it needs no key and this
# value does not affect it.
MODEL_PROVIDER=gemini

# Optional. Defaults to gemini-flash-latest, which always resolves to a current
# model. Pin a specific id here only if you need reproducibility — Google retires
# older ids for new API keys, so a pinned value can stop working.
#
# "You exceeded your current quota" on the free tier is a REQUESTS-PER-MINUTE
# limit, not a spent daily allowance — the error names a retry delay of a few
# seconds, and waiting clears it. The limit is counted per model, so switching
# ids clears it immediately too, which is the quicker fix mid-demo.
#
# Alternatives, all tested against a free AI Studio key on 2026-08-16 by asking
# for a full ticket listing. They are NOT interchangeable:
#   gemini-3.1-flash-lite  — pinned below. Rendered all six tickets, correct
#                            ellipses, finishReason=stop. The reliable choice.
#   gemini-3.7-flash       — highest limit seen (20/min) and what
#                            gemini-flash-latest resolves to today, BUT it
#                            truncated a six-ticket listing mid-response twice,
#                            stopping after two. Fine for short replies.
#   gemini-3.5-flash       — correct output, but only 5/min: the tightest limit
#                            measured, and easy to trip by clicking around.
#   gemini-3.6-flash       — DOES NOT WORK here: every request fails with
#                            "Request contains an invalid argument".
#   gemini-2.5-flash       — DO NOT USE on a new key: "no longer available to
#                            new users". Retired ids are exactly why the code
#                            default is the moving gemini-flash-latest alias.
# List what your own key can actually see:
#   curl -s "https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models?key=$GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY"
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite
